## 13. VERIFICATION PROTOCOL (applies to every milestone)

1. **Evidence or it did not happen.** Paste command + real output. A summary without output is a failed milestone.
2. **Red then green.** For every bug or rule, write the failing test first, show it fail, fix, show it pass.
3. **Search before you fix.** When a library or platform behaves unexpectedly, look up its documentation and cite the page in DECISIONS before changing code.
4. **Root cause only.** Grep every caller of a function before editing it. Fix once where all callers route.
5. **Surgical changes.** Do not touch unrelated files. List every file changed at the end of the session.
6. **No false confidence.** If you could not run something, say `UNVERIFIED-IN-AI-STUDIO` and give the human command. If a test is flaky, say so.
7. **Regression guard.** Each session starts by running `npm run check`. If it was green last session and is red now, fix that first.
8. **PROGRESS.md entry format:**
```text
## M<n> — <title> — <date>
Status: DONE | PARTIAL | BLOCKED
Changed files: …
Gate results: <command> → <output excerpt>
UNVERIFIED-IN-AI-STUDIO: <item> — human command: <cmd>
New decisions / OPEN items: …
Deviations from the prompt (with reason): …
```

